Program Purpose:
---------------

   The program creates a useable Character LinkedList. 

Compile/run:
-----------

    Compile and Run using the command "unit_test"


Acknowledgments:
---------------

    Had help from course staff through Piazza

Files:
-----

CharLinkedList.h: Interface for a simple Character LinkedList Class.

CharLinkedList.cpp: Implementation of a simple Character LinkedList Class.
    The default constructor for this class initializes an LinkedList to a size 
    of 0, and a capacity of 0. 

unit_tests.h: A unit testing file for the CharLinkedList Class. 
    Runs in conjunction with the unit_test framework to allow for testing of 
    individual functions.

Makefile: File to build the program.


Data Structures:
---------------

    This main data structure of this lab is an LinkedList, which is are nodes
    of elements that point to each other. Each Node stores the letter and 
    points to both the next Node in the list and the previous Node in the list.
    An advantage that this data structure provides is that the insertion and 
    removal of elements is relatively simple as it the other elements don't 
    need to be shifted. A disadvantage is that it takes longer to find the 
    element you're looking for because you must travserse the list until you 
    find what you're looking for.
    
    An interesting algorithm was the recursiveNodeAt function as it 
    recursively travsersed the entirety, each time subtrating 1 from the index  
    passed through until the index was 0 and the element was found. The 
    recurseReverse function was also interesting as it forced me to consider 
    how to add all the elements to a string in reverse order.


Testing:
-------

    I created some functions in the unit_tests.h class that tested attributes
    of my LinkedList functions to make sure they were working properly. These
    attributes included whether each function fufills its purpose and whether
    a function returns the proper error message given invalid input.


